{"text": "SLICKROCK INSURANCE EXCHANGE - CLAIM NOTES (recorded statement summary; audio on file 14 min 08 sec)\nClaim #: CR-AU-25-1184207     Policy: UT-PA-004418772     DOL: 11/01/2025 approx 5:40 PM\nAdjuster: Anders Folkestad, ext 4418            Statement taken 11/03/2025 by phone\n\nNAMED INSURED / DRIVER\nMarguerite Yoshioka, DOB 10-12-1959, UT DL 188441720\n2931 South 2300 East, Millcreek, UT 84109. Cell 801-555-0165. Prefers \"Peggy\".\nIV: 2020 Subaru Outback, VIN 4S4BTACC8L3204418, plate F18 4KT. Lienholder none.\nPlug-in telematics device on this vehicle, serial CRX-7720-4418-B (trip data requested).\n\nOTHER PARTY\nDriver Clayton Deveraux, age 17 per police report, permit/DL 204418772. Passenger: his sister Trinity Deveraux, age 14.\nCV: 2011 Chevy Silverado, plate 9KT 418, VIN ending ...G1187204, owned by the father. Carrier per exchange slip: Beehive State Farm Bureau Mutual, policy BFB-0091844-A.\n\nINSURED'S VERSION\nPeggy was northbound on 2300 East going home from a hair appointment. Light at 3300 South was green for her. CV turned left across her lane from the southbound turn pocket. She braked, hit CV at the right rear wheel. Est. her speed 30 to 35. Dry, dusk, headlights on.\nShe says the other driver got out and said \"I'm so sorry, I thought I could make it.\" His sister was crying and holding her arm.\nPolice: Unified PD, Ofc. Pruneau, case no. UP-25-204418. Other driver cited for failure to yield (she saw the officer hand him the ticket). Form DI-9 exchange slip in file.\nWitness: none she knows of. A man from the tire shop on the corner brought out a chair for her.\n\nINJURIES\nInsured: seat belt bruising across the chest, sore neck, left knee hit the dash. Went to urgent care that evening; x-rays negative. She mentioned she had a knee replacement on that side in 2021 and is worried about it. On blood thinners, so the bruising is extensive. PIP opened under Utah Code § 31A-22-309; med pay limit $5,000.\nOther vehicle: she believes the girl was taken by ambulance. Nothing confirmed. Both are minors, so contact goes through the parents only.\n\nVEHICLE\nIV towed by Jordan Narrows Towing & Recovery to their yard, 1450 West 2100 South, Salt Lake City. Tow invoice WF-118204, $285 plus $45 a day storage. Move it by 11/5. CCC ONE estimate pending; likely total loss, ACV range $19,500 to $21,000. Deductible $500.\nRental authorized 30 days at $40/day.\n\nOTHER\n- Insured asked whether her rates go up. Told her that is underwriting's call; liability looks 100% adverse.\n- She lives alone and does not drive at night since her cataract surgery; her son in Boise handles her email: yoshioka.kenji.r@treasurevalleymail.example. OK to copy him per her verbal consent on the recording at 11:20.\n- Subro: put Beehive on notice today.     AF", "kind": "Text file", "detail": "446 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Marguerite Yoshioka", "Clayton Deveraux", "Trinity Deveraux", "Pruneau", "Jordan Narrows", "Yoshioka Kenji"], "companies": ["Beehive State Farm Bureau Mutual", "Unified PD", "Jordan Narrows Towing & Recovery", "Beehive", "treasurevalleymail.example"]}, "topics": {"places": ["Millcreek", "South 2300 East", "3300 South", "Salt Lake City", "Boise"], "health": ["seat belt bruising", "sore neck", "knee replacement", "blood thinners", "urgent care", "x-rays negative", "knee hit the dash", "cataract surgery"], "sensitive": ["Clayton Deveraux", "Trinity Deveraux"], "names": ["Marguerite", "Peggy", "Clayton", "Trinity", "Jordan", "yoshioka.kenji"]}, "judged": {"candidates": 0, "requests": 0, "failures": 0, "places": [], "labels": {}}, "chunks": 2, "chunkErrors": 0, "topicErrors": 0, "importMs": 0, "modelMs": 0, "topicMs": 0, "detectors": ["email", "url", "ip", "iban", "card", "card_exp", "cvv", "ssn", "bn_ca", "sin_ca", "ein", "card_partial", "phone", "street", "dob", "age90", "date", "passport_dl", "routing", "credential", "device", "vin", "record", "account", "money", "zip", "postal_ca", "places", "region", "na